# Tech Stack

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router, TypeScript)
- **Database/Auth/Storage:** Supabase (Postgres, Supabase Auth, Supabase Storage for files like solar spec PDFs/Word docs)
- **UI:** Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- **Agent:** Google Gemini API with tool-calling (function calling), not a separate framework — keep it a direct API integration unless a real need for an orchestration library shows up
- **Hosting:** Vercel (app) + Supabase (managed backend)

## Folder structure conventions

```
/app
  /dashboard
    /kitchen-inventory
    /it-equipment
    /appliances
    /generator
    /solar
    /utilities
  /api
    /kitchen-inventory
    /it-equipment
    /appliances
    /generator
    /solar
    /utilities
    /agent          <- chat endpoint, tool dispatch
/lib
  /supabase         <- client init, typed queries per domain
  /agent
    tools.ts         <- tool definitions exposed to Gemini
    system-prompt.ts
/components
  /dashboard         <- shared table/form components
  /chat              <- chat UI components
/supabase
  /migrations
```

## Conventions

- One Supabase table (or small table group) per domain — see `020-data-model.mdc`.
- Every domain gets: a typed query module in `/lib/supabase`, API routes in `/app/api/<domain>`, a dashboard page in `/app/dashboard/<domain>`, and a matching agent tool in `/lib/agent/tools.ts`. No domain skips a layer.
- Use Zod for input validation on every API route and every agent tool — the agent will pass loosely-structured data from natural language, so validation is not optional here.
- No raw SQL from the chat agent, ever. It calls tools; tools call typed Supabase queries.
